<title>JAPAN: Hino Motors shares down on glum half-year earnings.</title>
<headline>Hino Motors shares down on glum half-year earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Hino Motors Ltd were lower in Wednesday afternoon trade, depressed by a glum half-year earnings result, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0400 GMT, the shares were down 72 yen at 968 yen, the largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.  </p>
<p>On Tuesday, Hino said its parent current profit in the six months to September 30, 1996 was 4.71 billion yen, down from 7.08 billion yen in the previous year.</p>
